{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
  "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "JOSHUA S. JOHNSON",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JOHNSON: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Eleventh Circuit held that annotations to Georgia's official code are categorically ineligible for copyright protection. That holding conflicts with a straightforward application of the Copyright Act's text and this Court's precedents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: This case --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JOSHUA S. JOHNSON",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JOHNSON: Well, I think it's different because the general assembly is not enacting individual legis -- annotations through bicameralism and presentment. So the annotations are first prepared by a commercial publisher, so by a contractor, and they do that subject to the supervision of the Code Revision Commission."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, but, counsel, aren't they approved? I thought they were at least approved as a whole by the legislature."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if the Commission is basically involved in -- in what should be in and what shouldn't be in to explain to people what the law means, why would that be copyrightable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. YANG",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think they're actually explaining what the law means. They're describing what other -- this is better than Callaghan because, in Callaghan, the reporter was at least superintended by the court, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would it make a difference if -- if, instead of the Commission, it were done by the legislature itself?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. YANG",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's right, because -- and look what the annotations are. Under this contract, they are intended to be comprehensive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could they copyright those and -- and charge for them and preclude others from copying them and disseminating them?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. CITRON",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it's useful to remember that the question Georgia presented in this case was whether the government edicts doctrine extends to documents that lack the force of law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I think one question that is -- I think Justice Ginsburg asked it, is -- is -- is some of your examples, they are government documents with a point of view, and -- and when you think about one of these annotation books, it doesn't look like it has a point of view. It looks like there are annotations of cases on both sides of an issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. CITRON",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are lots of cases that cite the annotations to the OCGA, as such, in Georgia for lots of different kinds of propositions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. CITRON",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So one of the cases that we point to where this -- an editor's note was cited is cited for the proposition that the -- the state changed the rule for when a breathalyzer test was admissible, and it did so retroactively to all cases that were pending on -- at the time that it was signed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You gave us a two-part test. The first part is whether it's a legal work. What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. CITRON",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0002-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And that causes Justice Harlan to write an opinion that says, even though Howell did that work on his own, you can cut and paste that text directly out of his book in order to republish a compilation of the laws because no one can own the laws."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "States",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c1f69047d1e05e17c8b21b2d051571ba5859f5ee3f825c9cbe015a818d5e4993",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c1f69047d1e0-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think the states have anything to fear. What they want is the official versions to exist. The official versions bear the states' imprimatur. They get to supervise what goes in them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1150",
      "confidence": 0.0,
